  "body": "### Summary\nAs a reader, I want a message's signature to be set apart by one thin line across the width of the message, not by the row of dashes « --------------- » HFR prints before it, so that the page reads cleanly (operator device feedback, 2026-11-10, after signatures showed again).\n\n### Facts\n- On the device, with « Afficher les signatures » on, each signature is preceded by a row of dashes on the same line (« ——————… »).\n- Legacy removes HFR's 15-dash string from the message before rendering: `HFRswift/Wrapped/LinkItem.m:74` @ `87fe0d1c`, `stringByReplacingOccurrencesOfString:@\"---------------\" withString:@\"\"`. It removes every occurrence, not only the one before the signature.\n- SwiftHFR does not port it yet: LOT-034 left it out until a capture shows the exact markup (#267, `host: mac`). The committed captures anonymize signatures to « Signature removed. », so none shows the separator.\n- `App/SwiftHFR/Reader/Resources/reader.css:133` already draws `border-top: 1px dashed` above `.signature`. The dashes text and that border add up.\n\n### Scope\n1. **Capture first:** #267, a message whose signature carries the separator, with the markup around it (inside or before `span.signature`, a `<br>` next to it). The capture must keep the separator and the markup, anonymized per FIXTURES.md.\n2. Drop HFR's separator in front of the signature only, in the normalizer (`MessageContentNormalizer`, LOT-034) or in the reader. Never drop dashes a member typed in the message body: an intentional difference from legacy, which removed every occurrence. Record it in the PR's `### Ledger` (`changelog` + GAP row).\n3. Draw one thin, solid, full-width hairline above the signature (`.signature` `border-top`, 1 device pixel, the separator colour of the theme), in light and dark and both message styles.\n\n### Acceptance criteria\n- On the #267 capture, the signature renders without the dashes and with the line; a body line made of dashes is kept.\n- Tests shown to fail without the change. Mac check on device.\n\nM4 (device feedback). Origin: parity (legacy removed the separator).\n\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code)_",
