   "body": "The capture is in PR #764 (`R267a`, #267). HFR's markup is:\n\n```html\n<span class=\"signature\"> ---------------\n\t\t\t<br />…signature…<div style=\"clear: both;\"> </div></span>\n```\n\nThe separator is the first text inside `span.signature`: one space, 15 dashes, a line break, then `<br />`. It never appears before the span. In the published fixture, \"Signature removed.\" replaces the member's text between the `<br />` and the clear div.\n\n**Not captured:** a message body with a line of dashes. The page has none, so the acceptance case \"a body line made of dashes is kept\" needs a unit fragment in this issue's tests. One option: an `R267a` message with a `---------------` line added to its `div#para…` body, marked as hand-built.\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code)_\n",
